[{:db/id "q-124224/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer/id #uuid "6eab3492-9d9d-5111-9619-ba096f1e7b6a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "7" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124224/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "037794be-432e-5662-97ac-f60f53a945b6" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124224/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "e2490baf-fe52-5d66-b93e-5369d7b86971" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124224/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" :answer/id #uuid "b2ca837f-ffa8-5ad5-9d65-7313bb5bae79" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-33" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124224/selection/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" :answer/id #uuid "53d010b3-2900-51ea-a5c2-021a4e0ec9de" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124224/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "50b86d78-627a-5db8-82a1-925eba6995b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124224/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" :answer-field/choices ["q-124224/selection/7f2aea1619f9c4cbe5384e0826442d82ebdb1ac614452244ced54b63c0c77efe" "q-124224/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" "q-124224/selection/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" "q-124224/selection/906fb68e52f34c93aaa89471be2f2ff4994dc9adb32c934377257fa64a54e307" "q-124224/selection/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124224" :question/id #uuid "5d8f9018-e49a-5dc6-b30f-3f20cff0c3d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-124224" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ a & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-9 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-1\\cdot (-9)-2\\cdot 4}[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-5 \\\\ -20\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ -4 & -9\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}5 \\\\ 20\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-4+(-9)+20=7.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124224/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0403251a-9491-5d04-ab5a-ed027024d0a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124224"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124238/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer/id #uuid "047d7661-add7-57f7-8f41-87c644bd2ecf" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "0" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124238/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" :answer/id #uuid "920e8c27-583f-51c9-9add-af7cd67a13d9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124238/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "b835c673-3eed-5efd-838b-a60cb3b41e8f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124238/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" :answer/id #uuid "28cabba1-5cfb-5518-8cb0-5a10bfd6138a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "1" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124238/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473" :answer/id #uuid "1d6efe97-0354-5d38-86f2-3083fb1cf506" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-4" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124238/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2bb3df9f-9bef-5c0a-a068-b10974aff81e" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124238/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" :answer-field/choices ["q-124238/selection/d971375f57c56d8a55a09f2b892e108787b055ceeadf005d7beed73e388cc467" "q-124238/selection/f80535409f78d0e1b5cd0ceb7e72783093e3cde8adf28a5032c83c6dc6b5e490" "q-124238/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-124238/selection/ad06fa8bb7e77edd4098e00237718855c96ba589745d004ae1aed5be17e6549c" "q-124238/selection/ae9425c9e204310ed598f729a242e0b42a2acbbf125bff30bc2080e10b8cf473"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124238" :question/id #uuid "a8bbef2f-90e2-5e6c-8433-de5f1145da6f" :question/math-academy-id "q-124238" :question/problem "The matrix form of the affine transformation $T$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nFind $a+b+c,$ given that the matrix form of the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is given by\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}a & -3 \\\\ 1 & b\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ c\\end{aligned}].\n$$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe matrix form of $T$ gives us the following information:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}-5 & -9 \\\\ 3 & 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{6\\cdot (-5)-(-9)\\cdot 3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{-3}[\\begin{aligned}6 & 9 \\\\ -3 & -5\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]-[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2 & -3 \\\\ 1 & \\frac{5}{3}\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ \\frac{1}{3}\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=-2+\\frac{5}{3}+\\frac{1}{3}=0.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-124238/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "0403251a-9491-5d04-ab5a-ed027024d0a4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124238"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124282/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" :answer/id #uuid "c93ca25a-7096-5f43-ac3d-973bfc1ec997" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-8" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124282/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" :answer/id #uuid "9a10a3bf-766e-59fe-94bb-cfa1e46c680d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-10" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124282/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer/id #uuid "e41b07b3-1d88-544f-a9f9-6c2505be6e17" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-6" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124282/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" :answer/id #uuid "60c0e35f-9689-5c9d-aa56-c17bf34f1bd2" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-12" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124282/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0" :answer/id #uuid "1de18a43-6575-5d60-8781-0dc5a9e52d9e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "5" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124282/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "b6643577-fa44-52f8-9cdb-dcd7c980bb11" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124282/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" :answer-field/choices ["q-124282/selection/34d6a116cfea25ad11008d41d6152ee565691a4dc671039515875488f5520d96" "q-124282/selection/5d022a88a643e97abec4d01dfce48411101475c0705a98f29f3a8e3560fb0616" "q-124282/selection/f853eeffac47c628af4a2b7e7b0ecd024652f548b0b0007bc18dba21ad82ad7c" "q-124282/selection/f509030681214332b5989836fe0af4b2eb5858d193e689fd8441dff5cd45ff45" "q-124282/selection/eadb4f132857861f1e64373661b9a01bc3625cc86bcffcc32659fc4899904fe0"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124282" :question/id #uuid "2bbe5c8f-5f13-5d77-bcba-0616b7c68af8" :question/math-academy-id "q-124282" :question/problem "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=2u-v+1,\\,y=9u-4v+3.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=y-4x+a,\\,v=by+cx+3,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v+1 \\\\ 9u-4v+3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2u-v \\\\ 9u-4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & -1 \\\\ 9 & -4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{-4\\cdot 2-(-1)\\cdot 9}[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4 & 1 \\\\ -9 & 2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x-1 \\\\ y-3\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-4\\cdot (x-1)+1\\cdot (y-3) \\\\ -9\\cdot (x-1)+2\\cdot (y-3)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}y-4x+1 \\\\ 2y-9x+3\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=y-4x+1,\\,v=2y+(-9)x+3.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=1+2+(-9)=-6.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124282/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b99071b9-d463-5e3e-9a0d-71711af836cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124282"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-124316/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer/id #uuid "c4f3a176-e1bf-58a5-8fad-eb248e09eb4c" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124316/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" :answer/id #uuid "219a0561-e4ee-5862-b114-650255f518a0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124316/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" :answer/id #uuid "af0e3026-8057-52ee-88cb-8ffa5e15f5c1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{1}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124316/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" :answer/id #uuid "d92c27be-527c-57fd-9e7e-653f5f39e7b0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "\\frac{5}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124316/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54" :answer/id #uuid "76c7b074-cbb9-519f-bd54-b758d8a9b28d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-124316/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "f0594b9f-57bb-5cf4-aa0c-07bd9fdbd552" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-124316/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" :answer-field/choices ["q-124316/selection/c087f5dc559272d193745a4428553203b94404f681d8529e6e619348c0528d10" "q-124316/selection/954f2b2ecf089f1c43903a74f4575cff67408acc792f8a71c271fa3076456a3b" "q-124316/selection/681a4b64a7bb464b7f554c4e26477e3547d3c60cd353fce5dda4ae108b1c4fa5" "q-124316/selection/4280bcd0914e40dbdc039bc97ee5d5baafd2654e75e9b692316d9c28c4842856" "q-124316/selection/62a6fd1cf465955cead36d661dcbed2f93206049c15d21d7eebcabb802d1aa54"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-124316" :question/id #uuid "be9e4836-1dc9-5427-b7c3-1f0fa45b5e48" :question/math-academy-id "q-124316" :question/problem "The affine transformation $T$ is defined as\n\n$$\nx=-2v-4,\\,y=u+4v+6.\n$$\n\nGiven that the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ of $T$ is\n\n$$\nu=2x+y+a,\\,v=bx+cy-2,\n$$\n\nwhat is the value of $a+b+c?$" :question/worked-solution "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nReversing the action of $T,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}Au+b & =x \\\\ Au & =x-b \\\\ u & ={A}^{-1}(x-b).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, writing our transformation in matrix form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v-4 \\\\ u+4v+6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}-2v \\\\ u+4v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & -2 \\\\ 1 & 4\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we calculate the inverse of $A:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{A}^{-1} & =\\frac{1}{4\\cdot 0-(-2)\\cdot 1}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}[\\begin{aligned}4 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u} & ={{[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{{A}^{-1}}\\cdot ({{[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}-{{[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 6\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}) \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2 & 1 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}x+4 \\\\ y-6\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2\\cdot (x+4)+1\\cdot (y-6) \\\\ (-\\frac{1}{2})\\cdot (x+4)+0\\cdot (y-6)\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}2x+y+2 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}x-2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding components, the inverse transformation ${T}^{-1}$ in coordinate form is\n\n$$\nu=2x+y+2,\\,v=(-\\frac{1}{2})x+0y-2.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\na+b+c=2+(-\\frac{1}{2})+0=\\frac{3}{2}.\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/hard :question/answer-fields ["q-124316/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "b99071b9-d463-5e3e-9a0d-71711af836cb"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-124316"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-162217/selection/99d5aeb2f87bf6ef13f130429773b8288f79a42bed11813730ac0875b5e7a025" :answer/id #uuid "f7b78b86-45af-57c1-a3f5-d5ad334a5415" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A triangle" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162217/selection/04a22f057dfb78cf7268b7e28949d343c0e04babc5e92513e1ecaee0279bd0e7" :answer/id #uuid "c8bf0bf9-8a03-5d14-965f-090519b9e41a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A parallelogram" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162217/selection/4e58580515bb45c045fd2f14cf2873f6efa6f0e2170ad5b45d216042e4ee999a" :answer/id #uuid "02dea30c-e499-5b84-9b33-e9bc84a9052a" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A point" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162217/selection/17289e1e8745422c797709f99e0edd5559d7531dceba3bb829f55cda3b5df310" :answer/id #uuid "13a809a1-3dd8-5138-821d-f17c0640dd3c" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A square" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162217/selection/c2d1a5ac4ed1170ec4ba684e8dd01cdba007525d6370ddfd38066ec585122318" :answer/id #uuid "a8dbf22b-d9d3-5d1e-be19-4070c40a3e22" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "A line segment" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-162217/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "e33aa621-7bf7-5e3c-85b4-e4e4c863cdb3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-162217/selection/99d5aeb2f87bf6ef13f130429773b8288f79a42bed11813730ac0875b5e7a025" :answer-field/choices ["q-162217/selection/99d5aeb2f87bf6ef13f130429773b8288f79a42bed11813730ac0875b5e7a025" "q-162217/selection/04a22f057dfb78cf7268b7e28949d343c0e04babc5e92513e1ecaee0279bd0e7" "q-162217/selection/4e58580515bb45c045fd2f14cf2873f6efa6f0e2170ad5b45d216042e4ee999a" "q-162217/selection/17289e1e8745422c797709f99e0edd5559d7531dceba3bb829f55cda3b5df310" "q-162217/selection/c2d1a5ac4ed1170ec4ba684e8dd01cdba007525d6370ddfd38066ec585122318"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-162217" :question/id #uuid "3018f96f-b9d5-5624-96d5-6e8a702124a0" :question/math-academy-id "q-162217" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/multivariable/14045422/assets/c1ee8bc2c212708ed583c709420a856b28f6e2129c24690a504b4716b2692aa7.png)\n\nConsider the affine transformation $T,$ given by\n\n$$\nx=u-2v+1,\\,y=2u-3v+1.\n$$\n\nWhat would be the image of the triangle shown above under the action of $T?$" :question/worked-solution "Recall that for any affine transformation \n\n$$\nT:u⟶Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix and $u$ and $b$ are $2\\times 1$ column vectors, we have one of the following three possibilities:\n\n- If $T$ is non-singular, i.e., when $det(A)\\ne 0,$ then the image of a two-dimensional object is a two-dimensional object. In particular, the image of a polygon with $n$ vertices is a polygon with $n$ vertices.\n\n- If $T$ is singular, i.e., when $det(A)=0,$ we have two additional subcases:\n\n- If $A$ has at least one nonzero entry, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a one-dimensional line segment.\n\n- If $A$ is the zero matrix, then the image of a two-dimensional object is a point on the plane.\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our transformation.\n\nThe given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}u-2v+1 \\\\ 2u-3v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}u-2v \\\\ 2u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNotice that the matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is \n$A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}].$\n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det(T) & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & -3\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot (-3)-2\\cdot (-2) \\\\  & =1 \\\\  & \\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we have a non-singular matrix. \n\nTherefore, $T$ is invertible and the image of the triangle under the action of $T$ is a triangle." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-162217/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e551b65-4116-58bc-b2bc-e536930c69b4"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-162217"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
